{
  "_note": [
    "The Cubeon Client mod's Minecraft version matrix, and the single source of",
    "truth for it: mod/build.gradle reads this file to know what to compile",
    "against, and cubeon/cubeonfriends.py reads it to pick which jar to install",
    "into a profile. Two hand-maintained copies of the same table would drift,",
    "and the failure mode of drift is a mod that loads into the wrong Minecraft.",
    "",
    "One bracket per Minecraft release, unlike the two it started with. Absorbing",
    "the standalone HUD mod that became Cubeon Client brought ~800 lines per era",
    "of HUD rendering that track Minecraft's own GUI classes closely - closer than",
    "the Cubeon button ever did - so a jar",
    "per exact version is what the HUD can actually be tested against. The ranges",
    "below are still consecutive and the newest is still open-ended, so a",
    "Minecraft released after this launcher falls into the newest bracket instead",
    "of silently losing both the button and the HUD.",
    "",
    "The line between the two halves of this table is not an API change - it is a",
    "NAMESPACE change. Minecraft up to 1.21.11 ships obfuscated, so a Fabric mod's",
    "compiled references have to be in Yarn names (which loom remaps to",
    "intermediary), and the mod's own Minecraft-facing sources are written in",
    "Yarn. Minecraft 26.x ships unobfuscated: there is no Yarn for it at all and",
    "the names in the jar are already the real ones, so those brackets declare no",
    "mappings and their sources use plain Mojang names. Fabric does no remapping",
    "at runtime, so no single jar can carry both sets of references.",
    "",
    "That is what the two overlay families are for:",
    "  api-yarn / api-mojang   the four Cubeon sources that touch Minecraft",
    "                          (CubeonClient, TabListTag, WorldPlayers, the tab",
    "                          overlay mixin), written twice, once per namespace.",
    "  hud-<variant>           the Cubeon Client HUD, one copy per HUD era (seven of",
    "                          them), because Minecraft's GUI classes moved",
    "                          between 1.20, 1.20.2, 1.21.9, 26.1 and 26.2 - and",
    "                          26.3 renamed InputConstants.Type.KEYSYM to",
    "                          KEYBOARD, so 26.3 needs its own copy of the",
    "                          keybind file even though its GUI is 26.2's.",
    "A bracket layers its api overlay and its hud overlay over the shared,",
    "Minecraft-free tree in src/main/java.",
    "",
    "Every bracket also needs Fabric API at compile time and at runtime: the HUD",
    "is built on HudRenderCallback / HudElementRegistry / KeyBindingHelper. The",
    "launcher installs Fabric API alongside this jar, and fabric.mod.json declares",
    "it under 'recommends' rather than 'depends' on purpose - a missing Fabric API",
    "must cost the player the HUD, never the game (see CubeonHudClient's guard).",
    "",
    "compile_against is the exact Minecraft version this key builds for. jdk is",
    "the toolchain that has to read that Minecraft's class files; the bytecode",
    "emitted is Java 17 for every bracket, because the mixin config declares",
    "compatibilityLevel JAVA_17 and Mixin refuses to apply a mixin whose class file",
    "is newer than that. A Java 25 JVM runs Java 17 bytecode happily.",
    "",
    "mappings: 'yarn' for the obfuscated releases (loom remaps to intermediary at",
    "build time). 'none' for 26.x and later, which ship unobfuscated - nothing has",
    "to be remapped, so nothing may ask for mappings.",
    "",
    "depends mirrors the absorbed HUD mod's '~<version>' so a future patch release",
    "of the same minor still loads the newest jar of that minor; the newest bracket",
    "is left",
    "open-ended ('>=26.3') so a 26.x released after this launcher still works.",
    "",
    "Anything below 1.20 is deliberately absent: the mod's sources use APIs that",
    "arrived with 1.20, so there is no jar to install and the launcher installs",
    "nothing rather than a mod that would crash on class load."
  ],
  "mod_version": "1.0.0",
  "loader_version": "0.19.5",
  "loader_min": "0.15.0",
  "jar_name": "cubeon-client-{version}+mc{key}.jar",
